Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedmip.shoddy — reckoner seed: mip.shoddy, converting at the
Rem bridge
Rem
Rem MIPPROBLEM, MIPSOLVE and MIPFIXED, all speaking the dict shapes
Rem seedsimplex.shoddy already established — which is why this seed
Rem includes that one rather than restating what a problem looks like.
Rem A keyboard with two spellings of "linear program" on it is a
Rem keyboard where MIPFIXED's answer does not go into LPSOLVE, and that
Rem round trip is the whole point of MIPFIXED.
Rem
Rem   { ("costs" list) ("a" matrix) ("rhs" list) } { 1 2 } MIPPROBLEM
Rem     -> { ("prob" problem) ("ints" list) }
Rem   MIPSOLVE
Rem     -> { ("status" s) ("x" list) ("cost" n) ("nodes" n)
Rem          ("iterations" n) }
Rem
Rem NO SHADOW PRICES ON THAT ANSWER, and the omission is the point.
Rem The duals of whichever node finished last are that node's
Rem sensitivities and not the integer problem's. MIPFIXED pins every
Rem integer where the search left it and hands back an ordinary
Rem problem, which LPSOLVE reads like any other and whose duals do
Rem mean something. The refusal is a door, not a dead end.
Rem
Rem NOTHING HERE ABORTS. mip.shoddy Errors on an Ints entry naming a
Rem variable that does not exist, and MipFixed Errors when handed a
Rem solution that never found an optimum to pin anything at; the LP
Rem underneath Errors on a problem whose matrix does not match its
Rem costs and right-hand side. All three are asked here first.
Rem
Rem A LONG SEARCH IS NOT AN ABORT, AND IT IS NOT CAPPED HERE EITHER.
Rem Branch and bound solves a linear program per node and may want
Rem many; the machine stops at a hundred thousand of them and answers
Rem MAXNODES. Wiring a smaller cap in at the keyboard would make this
Rem word answer something other than what mip.shoddy answers, which is
Rem the one thing a bridge must not do. LPSOLVE has the same shape of
Rem risk and the same non-answer to it.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "mip.shoddy"
Include "mps.shoddy"
Include "simplex.shoddy"
Include "sparse.shoddy"
Include "matrix.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seedsimplex.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- reading a problem dict back --------------------------------------
Rem LpFind and LpListNum are seedsimplex's, and using them is what
Rem keeps the two seeds agreeing about what a problem is.

Def MipProbRead(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(members)
            MipProbShaped(word, members)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(word & ": NOT A PROBLEM — BUILD ONE WITH LPPROBLEM OR MPSPARSE", at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def MipProbShaped(word As String, members As List Of Cell) As Result
    Select Case Pair(LpFind(members, "costs"), Pair(LpFind(members, "a"), LpFind(members, "rhs")))
        Case Pair(CutList(costsC), Pair(CutMat(a), CutList(rhsC)))
            MipProbTyped(word, costsC, a, rhsC)
        Case Else
            Err(word & ": NOT A PROBLEM — BUILD ONE WITH LPPROBLEM OR MPSPARSE", 0)

Def MipProbTyped(word As String, costsC As List Of Cell, a As Matrix, rhsC As List Of Cell) As Result
    Select Case Pair(LpListNum(word, CutList(costsC)), LpListNum(word, CutList(rhsC)))
        Case Pair(Ok(costs), Ok(rhs))
            MipProbSized(word, costs, a, rhs)
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem SpOptimize Errors on a problem whose matrix does not match, and the
Rem shapes are checked here for that reason rather than for tidiness.

Def MipProbSized(word As String, costs As List Of Number, a As Matrix, rhs As List Of Number) As Result
    If Length(costs) <> Cols(a) Then
        Err(word & ": COSTS HAS " & Str(Length(costs)) & " ENTRIES, A HAS " & Str(Cols(a)) & " COLUMNS", 0)
    Else
        If Length(rhs) <> Rows(a) Then
            Err(word & ": RHS HAS " & Str(Length(rhs)) & " ENTRIES, A HAS " & Str(Rows(a)) & " ROWS", 0)
        Else
            Ok(SpProblem(ToArray(costs), SpFromMat(a), ToArray(rhs)))

Rem ---- reading a mipproblem dict back -----------------------------------

Def MipRead(word As String, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckListArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(members)
            MipReadParts(word, LpFind(members, "prob"), LpFind(members, "ints"))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(word & ": NOT AN INTEGER PROBLEM — BUILD ONE WITH MIPPROBLEM", at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def MipReadParts(word As String, probC As Cell, intsC As Cell) As Result
    Select Case Pair(MipProbRead(word, probC), LpListNum(word, intsC))
        Case Pair(Ok(p), Ok(ints))
            MipReadInts(word, p, ints)
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & ": NOT AN INTEGER PROBLEM — BUILD ONE WITH MIPPROBLEM", 0)

Rem MipOptimize Errors on an index outside the variables, and a
Rem fractional index would name no variable at all.

Def MipReadInts(word As String, p As SpProblem, ints As List Of Number) As Result
    Let n = Length(Costs(p))
    If All(ints, Fn(k) => k >= 1 And k <= n And k = Floor(k)) Then
        Ok(MipProblem(p, ints))
    Else
        Err(word & ": AN INTEGER VARIABLE IS NAMED THAT DOES NOT EXIST — THERE ARE " & Str(n), 0)

Rem ---- writing the answers back -----------------------------------------

Def MipProbCell(p As SpProblem) As Cell
    LpProblemCell(ToList(Costs(p)), SpToMat(SA(p)), ToList(Rhs(p)))

Def MipCell(mp As MipProblem) As Cell
    CutList({ LpEntry("prob", MipProbCell(Prob(mp))),
              LpEntry("ints", CutList(Map(Ints(mp), CutNum))) })

Def MipSolCell(sol As MipSolution) As Cell
    CutList({ LpEntry("status", CutStr(Status(sol))),
              LpEntry("x", CutList(Map(ToList(X(sol)), CutNum))),
              LpEntry("cost", CutNum(Cost(sol))),
              LpEntry("nodes", CutNum(Nodes(sol))),
              LpEntry("iterations", CutNum(Iterations(sol))) })

Rem ---- MIPPROBLEM ---------------------------------------------------------

Def MipSeedProblem(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "MIPPROBLEM", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => MipMipproblem(vs)), "( problem ints -- mipproblem )", "A linear program whose named variables have to come out whole. ints is a LIST of variable positions, counting from 1; an empty one is just the linear program again.")

Def MipMipproblem(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(MipProbRead("MIPPROBLEM", Nth(vs, 1)), LpListNum("MIPPROBLEM", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(p), Ok(ints))
            MipMipproblemAt(p, ints)
        Case Pair(Err(w, at), other)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("MIPPROBLEM did not answer")

Def MipMipproblemAt(p As SpProblem, ints As List Of Number) As RckWork
    Select Case MipReadInts("MIPPROBLEM", p, ints)
        Case Ok(mp)
            RckVals({ MipCell(mp) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("MIPPROBLEM did not answer")

Rem ---- MIPSOLVE -----------------------------------------------------------

Def MipSeedSolve(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "MIPSOLVE", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => MipMipsolve(vs)), "( mipproblem -- solution )", "The best whole answer, by branch and bound. status is OPTIMAL, INFEASIBLE, UNBOUNDED-OR-INFEASIBLE, MAXITER or MAXNODES; nodes and iterations say what the search cost. No shadow prices — an integer problem has none. Use MIPFIXED for the ones it does have.")

Def MipMipsolve(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case MipRead("MIPSOLVE", First(vs))
        Case Ok(mp)
            RckVals({ MipSolCell(MipOptimize(mp)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("MIPSOLVE did not answer")

Rem ---- MIPFIXED -----------------------------------------------------------

Def MipSeedFixed(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "MIPFIXED", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => MipMipfixed(vs)), "( mipproblem solution -- problem )", "The linear program left when every integer is pinned where the search left it, as a pair of rows apiece. LPSOLVE it and its shadow prices are the sensitivity of everything else, given those decisions. Refuses a solution that never reached an optimum.")

Def MipMipfixed(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case MipRead("MIPFIXED", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(mp)
            MipMipfixedSol(mp, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("MIPFIXED did not answer")

Def MipMipfixedSol(mp As MipProblem, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckListArg("MIPFIXED", c)
        Case Ok(members)
            MipMipfixedParts(mp, LpFind(members, "status"), LpFind(members, "x"))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("MIPFIXED: NOT A SOLUTION — MIPSOLVE ANSWERS ONE")
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("MIPFIXED did not answer")

Def MipMipfixedParts(mp As MipProblem, statusC As Cell, xC As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(statusC, LpListNum("MIPFIXED", xC))
        Case Pair(CutStr(status), Ok(xs))
            MipMipfixedAt(mp, status, xs)
        Case Pair(other, Err(w, at))
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("MIPFIXED: NOT A SOLUTION — MIPSOLVE ANSWERS ONE")

Rem MipFixed Errors on anything but an optimum, and reads X at each
Rem integer position, so both are settled before it is called.

Def MipMipfixedAt(mp As MipProblem, status As String, xs As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If status <> "OPTIMAL" Then
        RckWorkBad("MIPFIXED: THIS SOLUTION IS " & status & ", SO THERE IS NO OPTIMUM TO PIN THE INTEGERS AT")
    Else
        If Length(xs) <> Length(Costs(Prob(mp))) Then
            RckWorkBad("MIPFIXED: THE SOLUTION HAS " & Str(Length(xs)) & " VARIABLES AND THE PROBLEM HAS " & Str(Length(Costs(Prob(mp)))))
        Else
            RckVals({ MipProbCell(MipFixed(mp, MipSolution("OPTIMAL", ToArray(xs), 0, 0, 0))) })

Rem ---- MPSMIP and MPSMIPLOAD ----------------------------------------------
Rem The MPS words live here rather than beside their siblings in
Rem seedsimplex.shoddy because what they answer is a mipproblem, and
Rem this seed is where that shape is written down. What they borrow is
Rem the validator: LpMpsCheckedMode is seedsimplex's own gate, told
Rem that integer columns are something these two can be handed.

Def MipSeedMps(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "MPSMIP", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => MipMpsText(vs)), "( text -- mipproblem )", "MPS text as an integer problem: the program, plus whichever columns the file marked whole with an INTORG marker or a BV bound. A file that marks none is simply a problem with nothing to branch on.")
    RckReg(s1, "MPSMIPLOAD", 1, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => MipMpsFile(vs)), "( path -- mipproblem )", "Read an MPS file and parse it as an integer problem, the guarded way throughout.")

Def MipMpsText(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("MPSMIP", First(vs))
        Case Ok(text)
            LpMpsCheckedMode("MPSMIP", text, False, True, Fn(t) => MipCell(ParseMpsMip(t)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("MPSMIP did not answer")

Rem Through TRYREADFILE rather than mps.shoddy's own LoadMpsMip, for the
Rem reason seedfile.shoddy gives: that word is ReadFile underneath and
Rem ReadFile aborts on a path that is not there.
Def MipMpsFile(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("MPSMIPLOAD", First(vs))
        Case Ok(path)
            MipMpsRead(TryReadFile(path))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("MPSMIPLOAD did not answer")

Def MipMpsRead(r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(text)
            LpMpsCheckedMode("MPSMIPLOAD", text, False, True, Fn(t) => MipCell(ParseMpsMip(t)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("MPSMIPLOAD did not answer")

Rem ---- the seed -----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedMip(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = MipSeedProblem(RckSeeding(st, "seed-mip"))
    Let s2 = MipSeedSolve(s1)
    Let s3 = MipSeedFixed(s2)
    MipSeedMps(s3)
